From f7c277b5b44a97437e7d1e192341364866699019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:00:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HiBreak: no 5G while Wi-Fi is the default network

On the HiBreak Pro Color, with 5G SA and Wi-Fi connected, incoming calls
stopped arriving after a few idle minutes; with Wi-Fi off, or on LTE,
they kept arriving. The cause is not established.

Per phone, track the system default network. Once Wi-Fi has been the
default for 10 s, mask NR (SA and NSA) out of the phone's effective
allowed network types and send them to the modem; the phone then stays
on LTE. As soon as Wi-Fi is no longer the default network, allow NR
again. The mask is runtime state in getEffectiveAllowedNetworkTypes(),
like the admin 2G restriction: no allowed-network-types reason (user,
power, carrier, enable_2g) and no subscription database value changes,
so nothing survives a reboot. It is not applied when it would leave no
LTE, and not newly applied during an emergency call or emergency
callback mode. Bigme HiBreak mt6877 only.

Kill switch: setprop persist.radio.hibreak_nr_off_on_wifi false (read
at every default network update; false allows NR at once). Logs in the
radio buffer under HBPC_NR_WIFI, once per change.

Wi-Fi counts as soon as it is the system default network, validated or
not. No change is applied while a call is active on any phone (state
not idle); it is applied once all phones are idle again.

Change-Id: Ife68d60be125d1ea76e35cff91a749d3434d2c27
---
 .../internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java      |   2 +
 .../telephony/HiBreakNrOffOnWifi.java         | 142 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../com/android/internal/telephony/Phone.java |  21 +++
 3 files changed, 165 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/HiBreakNrOffOnWifi.java

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java
index bf47b6d..aa8c94b 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.java
@@ -406,6 +406,8 @@ public class GsmCdmaPhone extends Phone {
         subMan.addOnSubscriptionsChangedListener(
                 new HandlerExecutor(this), mSubscriptionsChangedListener);
 
+        HiBreakNrOffOnWifi.start(this);
+
         logd("GsmCdmaPhone: constructor: sub = " + mPhoneId);
     }
 
